  chain="A convex lens is thicker in the middle and converges light, while a concave lens is thinner in the middle and diverges it -> parallel rays meet at (convex) or appear to come from (concave) a principal focus, and a lens has two foci -> the optical centre lets a ray pass undeviated, and the distance from it to the focus is the focal length",
